From: rhnvrm <hello@rohanverma.net>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:30:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf: use fixed array queries for priority metadata

Replace per-request IN-list query construction with fixed SQL and existing lib/pq array parameters. Preserve the 200-ID batches, nullable fields, acknowledgement filtering, replica and timeout/trace wrappers, and partial-failure handling.

Add real-store boundary, duplicate, legacy NULL and failure regressions, plus store and ordered-history benchmarks with positive metadata validation.

Mattermax-Patch: priority-ack-array-reads.patch
